<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Adaptive icon foreground: two overlapping tiles, the one behind cut into an
     L because the other sits in front of it, and the transparency checker on
     the front one. Proposal H of the icon browser, chosen as a placeholder.

     Geometry is COMPUTED, not hand written, and the source of the numbers is
     the browser that produced them. Two things about it are worth knowing
     before touching a coordinate:

     - The tiles are DISJOINT, on purpose. With the two outlines overlapping,
       the evenOdd sum split the front tile into two pieces separated by an
       empty band, and the rendered result looked nothing like the intent. The
       3dp gap between them is what reads as "in front", and it needs no
       overlap at all.
     - The L arm cannot take any pair of radii. The outer corner (9) plus the
       notch fillet (3) must fit inside the 12dp arm: with a fillet of 4 the
       vertical run went BACKWARDS by one unit and the outline overlapped
       itself. That defect is invisible on screen, because it happens along a
       straight segment: it shows up only by reading the generated path.

     Everything stays inside the safe circle of 66dp out of 108dp: the farthest
     point is 31.6 from the centre, against the 33 allowed. What falls outside
     is cut differently by every launcher.

     The colour is a resource, not a literal, so the glyph follows the device
     theme together with the background (values/ and values-night/). The
     monochrome layer reuses this same file: the system replaces the colour
     with its own tint and keeps only the alpha, so a flat single-colour shape
     is exactly what it wants, and a second file would only drift from this
     one. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/launcher_foreground"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M38,29 H55 a9,9 0 0 1 9,9 V38 a3,3 0 0 1 -3,3 H44 a3,3 0 0 0 -3,3 V61 a3,3 0 0 1 -3,3 H38 a9,9 0 0 1 -9,-9 V38 a9,9 0 0 1 9,-9 z M52,44 h16 a8,8 0 0 1 8,8 v16 a8,8 0 0 1 -8,8 h-16 a8,8 0 0 1 -8,-8 v-16 a8,8 0 0 1 8,-8 z M52,52 h10 v10 h-10 z M62,62 h10 v10 h-10 z" />
</vector>
